# REVIEW.md (copy to the repo root, link from CLAUDE.md)

The reviewer reads this first. It wins over generic checks.

## 1. What failure looks like here
- docs: it lies (says something the code does not do)
- config: it misroutes (right value, wrong target)
- billing / payments: wrong amount
- <area>: <how it fails>

## 2. Skip these paths
- generated code, vendor/, lockfiles, build output: <list repo paths>

## 3. Nit cap
At most 3 P3 nits per review. Drop the rest.

## 4. Evidence
Every finding cites path:line from the code. Never a guess from a name.
Tag each: Important / Nit / Pre-existing (present before this diff, reported, never blocks).

## 5. Summary
Starts with the finding count. If clean, say "nothing to fix" plainly.

## 6. Always-owner paths
Need the owner's look even when review is green. An agent approval never counts as the owner's.
- billing/payments
- auth
- CI workflow files
- deploy scripts
- DB migrations

## 7. Learned rules
One line each, with the date. Added by the implementer in the fix round when the same kind of finding appears twice.
